## Action-Level Expansion Model

The new expansion model is trained directly in persistence-action space.

For each action

\[
a
\in
\{1,2,3\},
\]

the model estimates whether the action belongs to the true minimum-regret safe-action set:

\[
y_t(a)
=
\mathbf{1}
\left[
a\in A_t^*
\right].
\]

The learned quantity is

\[
\hat p_t^{\text{safe}}(a).
\]

Only actions excluded by the primary gate are candidates for expansion.

This preserves the original high-precision set and attempts to recover false-negative safe actions selectively.

